# Ottili Coder is developed on Linux, macOS, and Windows. Git's Windows
# defaults check text files out with CRLF, which makes `prettier --check`
# report every file as unformatted because Prettier's `endOfLine` is `lf`.
# Normalizing in the repository and checking out LF everywhere keeps one
# formatting contract instead of a per-platform exception.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles and generated manifests are text but never hand-formatted.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf -diff

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail to execute; batch files need CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
